# Feature test scenarios

When adding or changing a feature:

- Read the requirement, approved plan, existing tests, and existing scenario document first.
- Use the `test-scenarios` skill to create or update `docs/test-scenarios/<feature>.md` alongside the code.
- Cover acceptance criteria, happy paths, validation, boundaries, security, data/integrations, and regression risks relevant to the change.
- Add automated tests only when the repository already has a suitable framework.
- Use only: `Planned`, `Automated`, `Passed`, `Failed`, or `Blocked`.
- Never mark a scenario `Passed` merely because it is documented. Include local test or screenshot evidence.
- Record unresolved assumptions and ask the user; do not invent business rules.
- Update scenarios when requirements or implementation behavior changes.
